      "content": "Those points they'll use seem pretty vague and high-level, honestly. It's all very \"save the planet\" and \"innovation,\" but it doesn't address the actual math of a business trying to stay afloat. When I bring up the specific cost increases and the risk to local jobs, does it feel like their arguments actually hold up against the reality of the industry, or is it more just moral pressure? Like, if you had to weigh the economic damage against these environmental goals, which side carries more weight in a practical sense?",
